# Local secrets for `npm run dev` (Miniflare, via
# @cloudflare/vite-plugin). Copy this file to `.dev.vars` (gitignored —
# never commit real values) and fill in real test-mode Stripe values.
#
# These are read at runtime via the Workers `env` binding
# (db/stripe-client.ts's resolveStripeConfig()) — this file has no effect
# on a real deployment; that platform's own secret store is authoritative
# in production (see docs/DECISIONS.md D-013).
#
# Where to get each value (Stripe Dashboard, test mode):
# - STRIPE_SECRET_KEY: Developers -> API keys -> Secret key (starts with sk_test_)
# - STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET: Developers -> Webhooks -> add an endpoint for
#   this app's /api/webhooks/stripe route, or `stripe listen --forward-to
#   localhost:3000/api/webhooks/stripe` for local testing -> signing secret
#   (starts with whsec_)
# - STRIPE_PRICE_STARTER: Product catalog -> Starter plan -> Price ID
#   (starts with price_) — must be a *recurring* (subscription) price to
#   match app/api/checkout/route.ts's `mode: "subscription"`.
# - STRIPE_PRICE_PRO: Product catalog -> Pro plan -> Price ID. Same rules,
#   and its amount must equal src/config/pricing.ts's `pro.monthlyPrice`
#   ($19/month recurring) or src/lib/price-integrity.ts closes checkout
#   rather than charging a figure the page never showed.
#
# Every plan in src/config/stripe.ts's STRIPE_PRICE_ENV_KEYS needs a value
# here; validateStripeConfig() fails closed on the whole set if one is missing.

STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_replace_me
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_replace_me
STRIPE_PRICE_STARTER=price_replace_me
STRIPE_PRICE_PRO=price_replace_me

# Magic-link sign-in (Resend). Without RESEND_API_KEY the sign-in route
# answers 503 and logs why, so local sign-in needs either a real key or a
# tail of the Worker log to read the link out of. Get a key at
# https://resend.com -> API Keys. The sending domain must be verified there
# or every send fails.
#
# AUTH_EMAIL_FROM is optional and defaults to
# `Ownword <no-reply@ownword.pro>`. Set it when the verified sending
# identity differs, e.g. a mail subdomain.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_replace_me
# AUTH_EMAIL_FROM=Ownword <no-reply@mail.ownword.pro>

# Humanization engine (M4-01). The engine ships with a deterministic,
# offline provider and uses it unless a model provider is EXPLICITLY
# selected — an API key sitting in the environment is never enough on its
# own (src/lib/humanization/provider-config.ts).
#
# Uncomment both lines to run rewrites through Claude locally. Leave them
# commented and the app behaves exactly as it does today, with no network
# call and no spend. `npm test` never reads either one: the provider takes
# an injected client, so the whole suite runs with no key at all.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: https://console.anthropic.com -> API keys.
# HUMANIZATION_EFFORT is optional (low | medium | high | xhigh | max) and
# defaults to `low`, not the API's `high`. Thinking tokens bill at the
# output rate, and a lower effort is safe here because the pipeline
# verifies every candidate before a customer sees it. Raise it only from
# what `npm run measure:cost` shows — the figure that matters is the
# verification rejection rate, not a read of the prose.
# HUMANIZATION_PROVIDER=claude
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-replace_me
# HUMANIZATION_EFFORT=medium
